\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Left: Example geometry of a rotationally stacked packed bed with a total of 18 layers L1 to L18 (reprinted from~\cite  {velten2026}). The surrounding cylindrical wall containing the flow is not shown to reveal the internal structure of the topology. Right: (top-left corner) Single element; then (from left to right and top to bottom), successively stacked beds involving one, two\ldots  six layers (L13 showing only the first layer, L18 all six layers tightly stacked on top of each other), with a constant rotation angle $\theta =30^\circ $ between two successive layers in the present case. The white regions shown in L13 to L16 indicate line-of-sight channels connecting directly inlet of the first element to outlet of the last element in a straight way; in the present case, such channels completely disappear after reaching L17, i.e., when stacking five elements on each other. The blue and red lines indicate the locations considered for PIV measurements in each layer and are used for later comparisons, with labels (Pos1, Pos3, Pos5, Pos7) in each layer. The regions delimited by blue or red lines shown for L14 correspond to straight through-passages connecting a lower module to the one above it~\cite  {velten2026}. For $\theta =30^\circ $, two such passages are found at positions Pos1 and Pos7 (white regions delimited by a blue boundary), and three passages at positions Pos3 and Pos5 (red boundary).}}{6}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:geometry}{{1}{6}{Left: Example geometry of a rotationally stacked packed bed with a total of 18 layers L1 to L18 (reprinted from~\cite {velten2026}). The surrounding cylindrical wall containing the flow is not shown to reveal the internal structure of the topology. Right: (top-left corner) Single element; then (from left to right and top to bottom), successively stacked beds involving one, two\ldots six layers (L13 showing only the first layer, L18 all six layers tightly stacked on top of each other), with a constant rotation angle $\theta =30^\circ $ between two successive layers in the present case. The white regions shown in L13 to L16 indicate line-of-sight channels connecting directly inlet of the first element to outlet of the last element in a straight way; in the present case, such channels completely disappear after reaching L17, i.e., when stacking five elements on each other. The blue and red lines indicate the locations considered for PIV measurements in each layer and are used for later comparisons, with labels (Pos1, Pos3, Pos5, Pos7) in each layer. The regions delimited by blue or red lines shown for L14 correspond to straight through-passages connecting a lower module to the one above it~\cite {velten2026}. For $\theta =30^\circ $, two such passages are found at positions Pos1 and Pos7 (white regions delimited by a blue boundary), and three passages at positions Pos3 and Pos5 (red boundary)}{figure.caption.5}{}}
